{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-smooth}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f451f94a2c2825244359aa8f3ad92fe7a4f9a2b0d65ff9665dc0b3315a9be84e", "source_text": "The smooth topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:962977d2e78d7007eb6435d41153e3a03d177fb62b390f95e12b8c0d6416ad18", "unit_id": "tag:021Y:title"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-section-etale-over-smooth}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60212ba9acd3893f3668f3e8d992452d575c9264b2b235c2e3ff854ea461fdcf", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we define the smooth topology.\nThis is a bit pointless as it will turn out later (see\nMore on Morphisms, Section <REF_0001>)\nthat this topology defines the same topos as the\n<ACCENT_0001>tale topology. But still it makes sense and it is used\noccasionally.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:68a99a0d764b1edd816a17c6e6e5eaa2863b3d3b2e57fa29d71d37e2e2a7fa69", "unit_id": "tag:021Y:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{f_i : T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$f_i$", "MATH_0005": "$T = \\bigcup f_i(T_i)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-smooth-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:283f9dea2be6a5f99e7e729bc3db42e6c914a1813f97c1b0e20c1ac32623e25a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:273c6a2e63fde74387d77761c4eda53c1043672ec4358bc71671803b049dd591", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>smooth covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes\nsuch that each <MATH_0004> is smooth and such\nthat <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5b05a3e1eeb607143477f900c8ebad845faa1879167ec90a76b98d96a32f13ca", "unit_id": "tag:021Z:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7cad3b502ecaedbd97cb39dd5b9eb2b82b27db05527ae55f02a266ecab60ca26", "source_text": "Any <ACCENT_0001>tale covering is a smooth covering, and a fortiori,\nany Zariski covering is a smooth covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:12b05784c61bce7da3cced8d995a914a6d48f1babaaff00c39baf2fa092a0163", "unit_id": "tag:0220:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-definition-etale}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:678875fe0cd89de7a2f8d91282065208f5d3efef70f927385ba4558524204b4a", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions, the fact that an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism is\nsmooth see\nMorphisms, Definition <REF_0001>\nand Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4be95c99fecf1ddf352b7fe1e01f022afed5cba6cfeab4cc02b67e65fe69277e", "unit_id": "tag:0220:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-site}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49426e16b2a071f5df0ca281f7d7592021c9d43c7bb94302ba6b7ebd4d1c3881", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNext, we show that this notion satisfies the conditions of\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fe60d7ff7dec91903335c151eda3e3489f64647b495bf10d622c43cc9afc0c89", "unit_id": "tag:021Y:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T' \\to T\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{T_{ij} \\to T\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0010": "$T' \\to T$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{T' \\times_T T_i \\to T'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-smooth}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e2cfe153eb45f4e05511defe14a0d0d67a3d5c22cf50aff12afe0aee9a4b79d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0eb615b26b88eb1d4ddd25ec6447e2f6fb50847a5ee3a94dc92d8a2d55b5c16b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0003>\nis a smooth covering of <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0005> is a smooth covering and for each\n<MATH_0006> we have a smooth covering <MATH_0007>, then\n<MATH_0008> is a smooth covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0009> is a smooth covering\nand <MATH_0010> is a morphism of schemes then\n<MATH_0011> is a smooth covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:27ae2064c8b1958f0cd6fe5340d4f788204197dea7f84041544e500ff9f71c36", "unit_id": "tag:0221:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "021Y", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:50e3cf58d6d7af0e2188b813b03f1252e2fa8cce224f0bee90b33d3cc0e75a8c", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:0221:proof"}
